# {{ project_name }}

Built with vflask for structured, maintainable Flask application development.

## Setup

The scaffold includes an isolated `.venv`. The first project command installs `requirements.txt` into it, and later runs refresh dependencies when that file changes. Set application secrets in `.env` before using integrations or deploying.

## Run the app

```bash
vflask run
```

Or run with your own external services:

```bash
vflask run --project-root . --no-services
```

## Create a module

```bash
vflask module create products \
  -f name:string:required \
  -f price:decimal:required \
  -f sku:string:unique \
  -r admin -r editor
```

## Project commands

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `vflask run` | Start the app and local services, choosing the next free port when needed |
| `vflask start` | Apply production migrations and start the Gunicorn server |
| `vflask db init` | Create tables and seed default roles |
| `vflask db migrate -m "add products"` | Generate a migration from model changes |
| `vflask db upgrade` | Apply pending migrations |
| `vflask test -- -q` | Run tests with additional pytest options |
| `vflask create-user <email> <name>` | Create a user; prompts for the password |
| `vflask push "feat: add module"` | Commit and push project changes |
| `vflask app -- <command>` | Forward any command supported by the generated app CLI |
| `vflask exec -- <command>` | Run an arbitrary project-local command without a shell |
| `vflask --help` | Show all framework and project commands |

## API docs

- Swagger UI: `http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/v1/docs`
- OpenAPI JSON: `http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/v1/openapi.json`

## Environment variables

Configure the following values before you deploy or run OAuth-backed features:

- `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`
- `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`
- `GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI`
- `EC2_SSH_KEY`

## Production checklist

- Use Alembic for schema migrations
- Store secrets in environment variables or a secret manager
- Run tests before deployment
- Use managed Postgres in production
- Keep OAuth redirect URIs exact
- Version releases using semver

This project is intended as a clean starting point for building real products with Flask, PostgreSQL, and a modern modular structure.
